# Git Ignore Files

# A .gitignore file (with that filename) tells git/GitHub which files
# and folders to not back up. Sometimes you have files in your local
# repository that you don't want uploaded to GitHub, because they are
# temporary, or secret, or specific to your personal computer.

# (These lines with the hash (#) at the beginning are comments.)

# For our project, we just need two things in our .gitignore:

# This is the folder of packages downloaded by npm (node package manager)
node_modules/

# This is the generated version of our site automatically built by our
# build tool (Vite)
dist/